From: Peeters Simon <peeters.simon@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH V2] Btrfs: cleanup: move node-,leaf-,sectorsize to fs_info
Date: Tue, 10 Jan 2012 14:05:06 +0100
Message-ID: <CAKyAS7uHabNKLWJE7gUjr3Q4weMF5_cqvbchJxqxPM6miOSvtQ@mail.gmail.com>
Mime-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=14dae93409cb0a483804b62c2a3e
To: linux-btrfs@vger.kernel.org, dave@jikos.cz
Return-path: <linux-btrfs-owner@vger.kernel.org>
List-ID: <linux-btrfs.vger.kernel.org>

--14dae93409cb0a483804b62c2a3e
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=ISO-8859-1

moved the node-,leaf-,sectorsize from btrfs_root to btrfs_fs_info
since we don't intend to allow different sizes between trees
also removed sectorsize from btrfs_block_group_cache because it now
can use the one in fs_info

updated all uses accordingly

please note in disk-io.c:
-static int __setup_root(nodesize, leafsize, sectorsize, stripesize,
-                                 *root, *fs_info, objectid)
+static int __setup_root(stripesize, *root, *fs_info, objectid)

Signed-off-by: Simon Peeters <peeters.simon@gmail.com>
